※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4407

※ Nothing calls a test but the runner, so there is nothing to give it and
※ nowhere for arguments to come from.  What it answers is whether it passed,
※ which is a truth value and nothing else: a status would be a second way of
※ saying the same thing, and answering nothing would leave the runner unable to
※ tell a test that passed from one that did not.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    0u6

@[test]
fn answers_the_wrong_thing() → u6:
    0u6
